  "descriptionMarkdown": "https://imgur.com/gallery/em-upcyler-XbjCSXg\n\nHi there, since I spent so much time on making this, I thought I might aswell share this blueprint and see how others think of it.\n\nWho is the target audience? Horders! Relentless and slow paced mad men grinding through this game like a drill through a mountain. Maybe you are a fellow Bigfoot enjoyer,  who wants to go big and has no idea about quality but the UPS problems finally force you to do quality.\n\nThis is fou you! This blueprint will get you higher quality from scratch in no time if you have the logistic capabilities to feed this system. \nThere is nothing you need to do, just choose the target items and go about whatever task you have ahead. \n\nThere is a short instruction imbedded in the blueprint aswell but I'll also explain it here:\nThere are essentially two diffrent requester groups. Primarily the requester in the bottom right will be responsible with feeding the recyclers with the target item in normal quality and secondarily all the others. \nI assume you have all the items you need in an abundance, just not in the desired quality. In case you have lets say uncommon grade items cuz u tried to do some quality already and want to get rid of it, you can also add a request to that requester in the bottom right.\n\nEven if you dont have the target item available, there is no problem at all, it will just delay things a bit becasue every other requester will be calling for all the needed componets in each quality to build your target item. This will happen no matter what and is highly recommended. This tri input system is the main reason to use this blueprint. You utilise the stock of unneeded items, the logistic capabilities of your factory and whatever the hell those damn recyclers give you, to get to your target item. \n\nIn case you didn't know, these both marvelous and demonic machines dont return the the full input value of the broken down item and sometimes not even the actual componets with wich the item was built, and thats why you will need the extra requesters. \n\nBut don't worry about any mess on the belts, any unneeded component will be ejected from the system, wich will mostly happen with copper based Items as far as I can tell. It would be wise to just slam some bot based assemblers with quality modules and return some copper wires into the cycle so your storage doesn't overflow with random quality coper plates. \n\nThe amount of recyclers is absolutely not mandatory, I've designed this so that the only thing that will fail is yourself and not the system.\n \nYou can forfeit any amount of machine you don't like or lack, nothing will ever get stuck thanks to the circuits. And if you intent to frankenstein with this you just need read through the combinators they all come with descriptions. \n\nYou can up and down grade almost anything however you want. just don't upgrade the inserter types. You can downgrade every inserter to yellows but if everything is even just a bulk it will break the flow.\n\nI highly! recommend starting by doing at least one quality module upcycler and further also for every single tier. Hell just upcycle modules and inserters exclusively, their value is  most important. And when you do get higher quality modules I recommend upgrading the recycler modules 1st.\n\nAnd i repeat, this system will if anything break your base, especially if your base like mine  also has a seconadry logistic network connection to every last item that is produced\n\nOh and the blueprint is build in a way that should fit 2 setups in most 100x100 cityblocks neatly.",
